  ('e1794143-ff30-4902-8415-fe0239135d8f', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 7), 'case-7', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Hamraie & Fritsch, Crip Technoscience: Hamraie and Fritsch, "Crip Technoscience Manifesto" (2019, shared by Dr. B). In March 1990 activists crawled up the U.S. Capitol steps, and Berkeley activists earlier chipped away curbs to make their own curb cuts. Read Bouyer charitably, as part of this tradition.', array['bdddbfe7-0300-4647-856c-5a483bc7abcd']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333301', 'bdddbfe7-0300-4647-856c-5a483bc7abcd', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('d2f22cd2-83b1-4830-9e4a-9a112453bba0', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 7), 'case-7', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Goodhart''s law: Goodhart''s law: when a measure becomes a target, it stops being a good measure. Steven Shavell (1984): after-the-fact lawsuits work badly when defendants are "judgment-proof" and the regulator knows the standards better than they do. Small, old businesses fail every test; chains and public agencies pass them.', array['919623da-3a2c-40e3-badf-1a5b81267db7']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333301', '919623da-3a2c-40e3-badf-1a5b81267db7', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('6db7a8b3-4851-4798-bb69-d108b2e3badf', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 7), 'case-7', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Derek Parfit, leveling down: Lola''s was sued over outdoor tables; removing them helps no wheelchair user. The Richmond closure produced zero ramps. Derek Parfit''s "leveling down" objection: making some worse off without making anyone better off is no gain in equality.', array['44357c83-89de-4426-8b9c-a1a7a9502e9f']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333301', '44357c83-89de-4426-8b9c-a1a7a9502e9f', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('de57c17a-0525-4d22-bbc6-e8938d77d2ee', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 7), 'case-7', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Young, social connection model: Iris Marion Young''s social connection model: responsibility for structural injustice grows with power, privilege and ability to act. The Richmond landlord controlled the structure. Teammate framing: "same charge, different penalty," as in sentencing. StopGap makes cheap ramps, so many fixes are affordable.', array['28f09b7a-e5d0-4b5f-8b74-add5301eca8d']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333301', '28f09b7a-e5d0-4b5f-8b74-add5301eca8d', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('2ebfb9d1-e7e1-4bde-a9fc-e090a6fcc9ae', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 7), 'case-7', 'Vivid example for this case', 'bounties are a normal tool: the federal False Claims Act pays whistleblowers, and California''s Prop 65 pays private enforcers. Condemning serial litigants while leaving public enforcement unfunded is incoherent.', array['f8f90c07-cacb-4086-b800-2e0eea5c692d']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333301', 'f8f90c07-cacb-4086-b800-2e0eea5c692d', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('9fb08205-d204-4634-81e6-6ca015bbcf2d', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Fact with citation', 'The Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM) opened in Cairo on November 1, 2025, holding 50,000+ artifacts spanning 5,000 years (Removes the "Egypt can''t care for it" objection)', array['03c3b0b2-37b3-420c-a99e-d80b45dd5a87']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '03c3b0b2-37b3-420c-a99e-d80b45dd5a87', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('77e7eb9b-1dfe-4f32-82ea-6725353bc9a5', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Fact with citation', 'The French found the Rosetta Stone in the 1790s; the British took it shortly after; it has been in London since (Acquired through war, not purchase or gift)', array['94b1c7f1-ada3-4f94-8701-d3d843eab09e']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '94b1c7f1-ada3-4f94-8701-d3d843eab09e', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('a24c9840-bb5f-474d-a280-37fa38e43983', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Fact with citation', 'The British Museum says Egypt''s government has made no formal request, and the British Museum Act 1963 "places strict limitations on returning objects" (The museum''s two shields: procedure and law)', array['5ea02162-8aee-45e9-93a3-cab362014811']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '5ea02162-8aee-45e9-93a3-cab362014811', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('9efb3581-a583-49b8-a953-750c47fde592', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Fact with citation', 'Greece asked for the Parthenon Marbles in the 1980s; the Act helped block it; talks continue, with Greece offering loans to "fill the void" (A model for a deal that leaves London something)', array['91f48e68-8afc-4625-8124-002a4e2cdb98']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '91f48e68-8afc-4625-8124-002a4e2cdb98', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('0fc8650e-a723-4ecb-9339-fcb46ec78c7c', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Fact with citation', 'Uganda and Ghana received objects from England on loan in 2024, without ownership (Loans without title are today''s compromise)', array['9c8ac8d9-73ff-4813-a49e-805de29f4ee2']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '9c8ac8d9-73ff-4813-a49e-805de29f4ee2', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('ae761140-09e6-4502-890a-f0a2354c9334', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Fact with citation', 'UCLA''s Fowler Museum voluntarily returned seven artifacts to Ghana in 2024, citing an ethical duty for objects taken violently or coercively (Institutions can act first)', array['a87479ae-5628-4ca1-82ff-edb5c129eec9']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', 'a87479ae-5628-4ca1-82ff-edb5c129eec9', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('f31d53a0-9a00-4f7e-a722-f14735e2d7d7', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Fact with citation', 'NAGPRA (1990, recently updated) makes museums, not tribes, start repatriation, with consent needed before display (The holder carries the burden of acting)', array['cf3061e0-6250-477b-a208-8e6fec371d08']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', 'cf3061e0-6250-477b-a208-8e6fec371d08', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('00f17471-a98b-4a2e-9725-9f6c5de4fdfa', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Fact with citation', 'Deaccessioning costs staff time and money and, some say, erodes "public trust" (The museum''s strongest practical points)', array['85f02411-f0d4-44cb-8c0d-00fe267a453e']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '85f02411-f0d4-44cb-8c0d-00fe267a453e', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('9d8a3034-9dbc-4ed5-bb64-9006747ae767', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Nozick, entitlement theory: Robert Nozick''s entitlement theory (1974), a pro-property theory, condemns this title: a handover from the army that took it to the army that took it from them. An Ottoman admiral''s signature isn''t Egyptian consent.', array['b518c53e-b1b7-4cbf-a175-07d8de46ac8f']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', 'b518c53e-b1b7-4cbf-a175-07d8de46ac8f', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('a29f7fc8-4ad5-4ab1-9c90-f35fbeaec2c9', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Kant, test: Kant''s test: if everyone kept what they took whenever they judged themselves better caretakers, ownership would belong to the strongest and best-funded, destroying the property claim the museum relies on. And "we know better how to care for your heritage" is paternalism that treats Egyptians as less than equal moral agents.', array['a4d55107-b5e8-4087-ae09-bd2ed59de29a']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', 'a4d55107-b5e8-4087-ae09-bd2ed59de29a', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('42afdec7-39a7-4d80-b976-71d0784dfa4d', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Young, parameters: Iris Marion Young''s parameters (power, privilege, interest, collective ability) put a heavy duty on a wealthy national institution. W.D. Ross lists reparation among our basic duties.', array['7e7c3ee4-bac8-4c11-ba5b-6b0426156ca3']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '7e7c3ee4-bac8-4c11-ba5b-6b0426156ca3', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('c5b7e9b8-1746-4ffc-95fc-b9d035a7b378', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Universal-museum argument: the universal-museum defenders (Appiah, Cuno) rest their case on care and access. With the GEM open, care is a tie, and a tie goes to where the object was made and is part of living identity. The 2002 "universal museum" declaration was signed by the directors of the museums holding contested objects: no one should judge their own case.', array['fe137ba3-8a9c-41ce-b390-b2b3affd62c8']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', 'fe137ba3-8a9c-41ce-b390-b2b3affd62c8', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('2144ec92-efcb-4f0b-a1af-638a26a45198', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 9), 'case-9', 'Vivid example for this case', 'the Benin lesson: after Germany returned bronzes to Nigeria in 2022, a 2023 decree vested ownership in the Oba, raising public-access fears, so public display should be written into the transfer. In 2009 Egypt suspended cooperation with the Louvre until it returned five fresco fragments, which France did within weeks. An early, voluntary return buys loans and goodwill; a forced one buys nothing.', array['0ca07e79-1531-43ec-bd25-6c0fc02895b6']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '0ca07e79-1531-43ec-bd25-6c0fc02895b6', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('831aa892-29ed-48b2-9578-b9ea2ab7b308', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 10), 'case-10', 'Fact with citation', 'India''s Delhi High Court ordered search engines to de-index records of people who were acquitted or discharged; the court records themselves stay public (*The Hindu*, June 1, 2026)', array['9910e46c-3763-416a-960a-d79ff29cdce8']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', '9910e46c-3763-416a-960a-d79ff29cdce8', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('7a80c21c-3221-4dae-8c52-f348d1c2c7b5', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 10), 'case-10', 'Fact with citation', 'The right to be forgotten is distinct from privacy: it concerns information that was once legitimately public (Case text)', array['a0b7d1df-8cea-4899-8677-2ea091e2ea57']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', 'a0b7d1df-8cea-4899-8677-2ea091e2ea57', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('5710d90f-4b0c-4952-a44b-02e2cf428517', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 10), 'case-10', 'Fact with citation', 'Online records can cost people jobs and housing long after an acquittal (Case text)', array['26d1625f-49d0-415e-b51e-2e034abf4572']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', '26d1625f-49d0-415e-b51e-2e034abf4572', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('6bbd2c33-3485-47b2-b35c-0852edf98d62', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 10), 'case-10', 'Fact with citation', 'The case links the right to harms like revenge porn, where information was never consented to (Case text)', array['0ff7d360-872a-4328-94a7-663e4933c1d6']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', '0ff7d360-872a-4328-94a7-663e4933c1d6', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('17d6f903-ac85-4d26-a639-25324b4466ea', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 10), 'case-10', 'Fact with citation', 'Graham Platner, a U.S. Senate candidate, deleted old Reddit posts that were archived and resurfaced anyway (CBS News, October 16, 2025)', array['deb2770a-fe11-4d27-810e-7a6678d3454c']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', 'deb2770a-fe11-4d27-810e-7a6678d3454c', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('3b00fdc1-3b20-4c6d-8ca7-346f169bee76', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 10), 'case-10', 'Fact with citation', 'Proponents: people change and deserve a fresh start. Opponents: the public, press and employers need accurate history (Case text)', array['c19d9d9c-3e5a-4f6b-a4a6-e54f22885c1f']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', 'c19d9d9c-3e5a-4f6b-a4a6-e54f22885c1f', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('beef5356-68e2-4b89-a288-c4daca3913f5', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 10), 'case-10', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Mill, harm principle: Mill''s harm principle cuts both ways: the information harms the person while serving no one''s safety. Restorative justice (the team noted South Africa''s truth-and-reconciliation model) aims at return to the community, not permanent exclusion.', array['c710dcee-2a57-4447-bf5d-3ac8df279a44']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', 'c710dcee-2a57-4447-bf5d-3ac8df279a44', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('dd415933-6105-4298-b142-fffce1468cb2', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 10), 'case-10', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Kant: Kant: treating someone as permanently defined by an accusation denies their capacity to change.', array['77fa0a8b-49d1-4157-8fa1-fa9fff79cd0f']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', '77fa0a8b-49d1-4157-8fa1-fa9fff79cd0f', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('5c43384e-0571-4e6f-9564-f3c3173bf5e3', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 10), 'case-10', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Waldron, dignity: accountability requires a reliable record; Jeremy Waldron''s work on dignity explains why the harm of exposure must be weighed against the public''s need, not ignored.', array['14f12f22-1561-4098-9925-fdce2f97250f']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', '14f12f22-1561-4098-9925-fdce2f97250f', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('69faade6-6fb7-460a-9552-58be10eddcee', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 11), 'case-11', 'Fact with citation', 'Cervical cancer causes about 660,000 cases and 350,000 deaths a year; the HPV vaccine can prevent most of it, but cost and access are barriers (Case text)', array['eaec575d-116f-4ada-81f7-86a25592ba8a']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', 'eaec575d-116f-4ada-81f7-86a25592ba8a', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
