  ('fe664218-3cc0-46af-930e-c6d058d1e372', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 13), 'case-13', 'Fact with citation', 'For liability: dehumanizing rhetoric raises the odds; large audiences give outsized influence; lack of immediacy gives plausible deniability (Case text)', array['cb2219d7-abd7-48ec-87be-e3b9e20f1ecd']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', 'cb2219d7-abd7-48ec-87be-e3b9e20f1ecd', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('2b4b4360-9f55-4f5e-9503-a648670311a3', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 13), 'case-13', 'Fact with citation', 'Against: liability carves exceptions into free expression, which protects diverse views and even exaggeration and lies (Case text)', array['5996a058-c8e4-4fff-94dc-4d4164274944']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '5996a058-c8e4-4fff-94dc-4d4164274944', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('8dc07d9a-3e6b-4e00-b736-c69b84adf3b8', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 13), 'case-13', 'Fact with citation', '*Whitney v. California* (1927) upheld punishing some harmful speech; *Brandenburg v. Ohio* (1969) protected speech unless directed to inciting imminent lawless action and likely to produce it (274 U.S. 357; 395 U.S. 444)', array['bf209617-b5da-45b7-925b-2d1ca4e0d84f']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', 'bf209617-b5da-45b7-925b-2d1ca4e0d84f', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('d2a1cab0-908d-40d7-8721-0dcab8db3978', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 13), 'case-13', 'Fact with citation', 'Hypothetical: a popular figure dehumanizes a group at a rally and calls for action to impede a political event happening within hours, nearby. Is that "imminent"? (Case text)', array['289d85d4-293c-412f-ba0b-ce947c06fc3f']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '289d85d4-293c-412f-ba0b-ce947c06fc3f', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('e2c1dcdc-b6e4-4849-96b0-1bbbda52e491', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 13), 'case-13', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Derek Parfit, mistakes in moral mathematics (1984): Derek Parfit''s "mistakes in moral mathematics" (1984): it''s a mistake to ignore small chances of great harm spread across many people. We blame a drunk driver for the risk they impose even on nights they don''t crash. The speaker controls the curve, not which point on it acts.', array['61a6d3b5-591f-4ea2-b07e-1f7db4cac615']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '61a6d3b5-591f-4ea2-b07e-1f7db4cac615', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('9451d2f6-5c1b-4950-b2e1-b492eb238b0a', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 13), 'case-13', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Waldron, The Harm in Hate Speech: Kant''s humanity formula (the team''s lead framework): the speaker treats listeners as tools, betting one will act, and targets as obstacles. Jeremy Waldron''s *The Harm in Hate Speech* (2012): it attacks a group''s assurance of equal standing. Austin''s speech-act theory: labeling a group as vermin is an act of marking them. The 2003 Rwanda media convictions show rhetoric can be a recognized cause of mass violence.', array['75bbf017-beb1-49b0-aeda-4337905bab91']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', '75bbf017-beb1-49b0-aeda-4337905bab91', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('5cf9ea6a-9ea8-4b91-bcb8-f6cd60d25152', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 13), 'case-13', 'Vivid example for this case', 'Martin Luther King Jr. paired mass audiences with explicit, repeated commitments to nonviolence. Major speakers have speechwriters and rehearse; "I can''t control how people interpret me" is weak from someone who crafts every line.', array['be73693c-1ba6-40eb-b272-8d91462d45b3']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333302', 'be73693c-1ba6-40eb-b272-8d91462d45b3', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
