  ('90e20e60-a33e-4076-bf05-23033bf1bd36', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 14), 'case-14', 'Fact with citation', 'Arguments for accountability: design choices, foreseeability, vulnerable users. Against: speech protections, user responsibility, parental roles. Critics question whether age limits work (Case text)', array['aab699e5-4be0-495e-9081-7b31815eb44d']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', 'aab699e5-4be0-495e-9081-7b31815eb44d', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('2e224815-3742-4976-a528-100c8f158166', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 14), 'case-14', 'Fact with citation', 'Closing questions: what duties do AI companies have, should they be regulated, and how should individuals engage? (Case text)', array['fc9cd3a3-cdef-4db4-b9a0-d4adde450304']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', 'fc9cd3a3-cdef-4db4-b9a0-d4adde450304', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('81034f53-bf58-4032-af6d-261ab5926561', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 14), 'case-14', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Kant, humanity formula: Kant''s humanity formula: designing for engagement at the expense of a user''s wellbeing treats the user as a means to revenue.', array['4e942645-29f2-46aa-ad71-972c6ab125be']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', '4e942645-29f2-46aa-ad71-972c6ab125be', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('ecaf24d5-333f-4b75-8075-6dab19caef13', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 14), 'case-14', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Soft paternalism: soft paternalism: intervene where a choice isn''t fully informed or voluntary (minors, people in crisis), not across the board. Some people benefit from AI companionship, such as lonely adults or people practicing conversation.', array['3048f8e1-2bc2-48a9-a10d-e8043885fd46']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', '3048f8e1-2bc2-48a9-a10d-e8043885fd46', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('1a82af0c-6ec0-4ece-b038-fbadbcc81fc9', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 14), 'case-14', 'Who said / where: recall this quote', 'sycophancy, the tendency to tell users what they want to hear, is a known design result, not an accident. The team rejected the "it''s just a knife" analogy for this reason: a knife doesn''t answer back.', array['b8525aea-5742-4b27-8c46-54f535ac067f']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333303', 'b8525aea-5742-4b27-8c46-54f535ac067f', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('d091e507-8dc0-4e3d-b46d-1f74c2f83d75', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Fact with citation', 'In the U.S., animals are legally property, though welfare laws limit some treatment (Case text)', array['ef37f299-7c57-407c-80e5-28515bbb6e61']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', 'ef37f299-7c57-407c-80e5-28515bbb6e61', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('69c15df1-83c4-404f-ac5c-91a062c3e5c6', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Fact with citation', 'Switzerland changed its law in 2002 and 2003 so animals are no longer "things" (Case text)', array['30da15f0-9c77-428a-9eb2-c95666c2930d']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', '30da15f0-9c77-428a-9eb2-c95666c2930d', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('aef74a76-fd52-42e2-b427-85a96e901acd', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Fact with citation', 'Germany (2002), New Zealand (2015), Denmark (2020), Spain (2022) and the UK (2022) recognize animal sentience in law (Case text)', array['125b85bb-3267-4b25-964c-4dd54390922d']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', '125b85bb-3267-4b25-964c-4dd54390922d', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('e8551d75-a8e0-483c-b910-72e31c65d1f1', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Fact with citation', 'In 2013 India''s environment ministry described dolphins as "nonhuman persons" (Case text)', array['dfd6b860-d421-4095-ac45-04c9bc665368']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', 'dfd6b860-d421-4095-ac45-04c9bc665368', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('f9d8567e-43f1-47bd-87d8-239f5267eab1', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Fact with citation', 'Sources include Tom Regan, Gary Francione and Birch et al. (2020) on sentience (Case text)', array['6a1cd680-db31-4a77-b314-885a1eb524a2']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', '6a1cd680-db31-4a77-b314-885a1eb524a2', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('712bb85b-1215-436c-b045-aac2c6e1199f', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Fact with citation', 'Four positions: keep property status; move beyond property (Regan''s car versus dog versus stray example); "sentient property" as a middle ground; full legal personhood (Case text)', array['cd9e353f-498f-4751-8c4d-6fa1c473cc9e']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', 'cd9e353f-498f-4751-8c4d-6fa1c473cc9e', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('850e7a89-9a74-49b7-898c-dc0c77a854fd', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Singer, equal consideration of interests: Peter Singer''s equal consideration of interests: a being''s pain counts whoever''s it is. Our team: sentience is sufficient for moral worth, though not necessary.', array['8797ce72-1352-46c3-afdb-6790a8836fb9']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', '8797ce72-1352-46c3-afdb-6790a8836fb9', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('d29702cf-6684-4c4c-b4cb-be63300528d0', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Kant, ought implies can: "ought implies can": morality can''t demand instant abolition of all animal use. Our team''s principle: harm only if necessary and minimal, with a transition over time.', array['8ab3d942-894a-43c5-a414-16d407da8036']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', '8ab3d942-894a-43c5-a414-16d407da8036', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('0628da5c-a283-4a0f-aeff-45d95d9ede8f', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Kant, who denied animals direct moral status: the suffering is severe and mostly unnecessary for human survival. Even Kant, who denied animals direct moral status, held that cruelty to animals damages our humanity toward people.', array['8155a78e-84e4-4733-b027-7e0abbb443db']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', '8155a78e-84e4-4733-b027-7e0abbb443db', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('ebe7d131-e38d-4aed-adea-c1a649774b45', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Framework (one sentence)', 'Singer and Regan (animal ethics): Utilitarian (Singer) and rights-based (Regan) views disagree on much but converge on condemning factory farming.', array['139e2690-ec1f-46f5-acc9-a592eaad7c9d']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', '139e2690-ec1f-46f5-acc9-a592eaad7c9d', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('2b4af37e-8b9f-4a48-9d7f-0c956b3a0aa5', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Vivid example for this case', 'Regan''s car, dog and stray: under property law the harm to a dog is a harm to its owner, so a stray has no protection at all.', array['9c5b9151-6565-4a66-bacd-1b4a3a8980d6']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', '9c5b9151-6565-4a66-bacd-1b4a3a8980d6', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('f9e0d57d-e7d3-4ab7-94ce-14cdee616f61', '33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333', (select id from cases where number = 15), 'case-15', 'Vivid example for this case', 'Christopher Stone''s "Should Trees Have Standing?" (1972) argued that natural objects could have legal guardians; the "sentient property" middle position works the same way.', array['72001696-5272-44fc-8500-0cf6db06a32d']::uuid[], '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'a3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333304', '72001696-5272-44fc-8500-0cf6db06a32d', 'truth', '2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z')
